From 75dfa6cff8f2d3d2a37eecc5af3ff5a28a48c56e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "google-labs-jules[bot]"
 <161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 07:49:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Implement Fixed-Tile Redraw unification and layout
 optimizations

- Implement scale-aware fixed-tile redraw across BeOS, Windows, GTK, Qt, and Monkey frontends.
- Enhance Windows fixed-tile redraw with robust GDI hardware clipping (SaveDC/RestoreDC/IntersectClipRect).
- Fix QuickJS DOM bridge use-after-free during engine and context teardown by snapshotting keys and disabling the lookup map.
- Optimize Incremental Layout by skipping flag propagation when ancestors are already marked for reflow.
- Implement dirty rectangle accumulation for 'old' positions in `box_mark_dirty` and ensure removal invalidation in `box_unlink_and_free`.
- Standardize on `MAX`/`MIN` macros in Monkey frontend and include `wisp/browser.h`.
- Correct Qt off-by-one caret clipping boundary.
- Implement scale-aware `browser_get_tile_size` utility.

Co-authored-by: tonestone57 <216575567+tonestone57@users.noreply.github.com>
